# Baseline for dev/check_upstream_deletions.py — the reverse-direction audit.
#
# Format matches .symbol-exclusions: `path/glob::symbol_glob  # reason`, or
# `path/glob  # reason` for a whole file. Every entry MUST carry a reason; the
# script refuses to run otherwise. "Unreviewed" is not a reason — say what you
# established and how.
#
# What this file is for: this audit asks the mirror of the other checks — what
# content did upstream DELETE that we still carry? Every hit is either FORK (we
# added it; keep) or STALE (upstream removed it; delete ours). See AGENTS.md.
#
# Almost every entry below is the *second half of a dropped commit*. When upstream
# moves or renames a symbol A -> B and our merge resolution drops the B half, we
# keep A. `check_upstream_symbols.py` then reports B as "missing" and this script
# reports A as "we kept something upstream deleted" — two halves of one event that
# neither check can connect. These resolve when the owning commit is restored;
# delete the entry then, do not let it rot.
#
# Already resolved by acting on this audit's first run (kept here as the record):
#   models/cache.py::SlidingWindowCache, ::StaticKVCache, ::get_max_cache_shape
#     Deleted. Upstream removed all three in a492e47d "Consolidate caches + RoPE
#     handling (#1494)" (ancestor of both HEAD and upstream/main). They had ZERO
#     references anywhere outside cache.py — dead stale upstream code. AGENTS.md
#     had listed two of them as protected "fork-only classes", which is exactly
#     the trap it warns about elsewhere.
#   utils.py::apply_forced_token (+ its 4 tests)
#     Renamed. 565ca595 "Rename forced token consumer" renamed it to
#     pop_forced_token_id and changed the contract from
#     (next_y: mx.array) -> mx.array to () -> Optional[int]. We had the old name
#     only; 7 .symbol-exclusions entries excused the "missing" new one.

# --- mlx_vlm/apc.py
# RESOLVED 2026-08-09: 8422ece8 (#1638) restored, and _merge_arrays_cache_entries
# DELETED as stale. It had zero references anywhere in the tree, upstream does not
# define it at all, and our copy is byte-identical to upstream's last pre-deletion
# version — so the fork never touched it: STALE, not FORK, by the conclusive test in
# AGENTS.md. Its only caller went away with 8422ece8's refactor. Same shape as
# models/cache.py::SlidingWindowCache.
#
# The rest of that commit is now in: dispatch.py's ~113-line inline APC lookup block
# became an 8-line `_apc.apc_lookup_plan(...)` call, `apc_extra_hash` now goes
# through `semantic_extra_hash` (see below), and ar.py's `_apc_prompt_cache_for_store`
# delegates to `snapshot_prompt_cache_row`.
#
# Two real bugs came out of it, neither with a failing test:
#   * The APC cache key was `tenant_scoped_hash(tenant, image_hash)` — audio, video,
#     inputs_embeds and masks were NOT in the key, so two requests differing only in
#     audio would share a prefix cache and reuse KV computed for other media.
#   * `_apc_prompt_cache_for_store` returned the LIVE prompt cache for single-row
#     batches instead of a clone, so a stored "checkpoint at N tokens" kept growing
#     as generation continued; it also never dequantized quantized layers.

